        "id": 1983105
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T01:36:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry. I think the handler_running can\u0027t be set to 0 if the btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_audio_queue is not empty. \nThe root cause is that when loop dequeue from rx_audio_queue is running, handler_running is set to 0, stack will call more DoInThread() for btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer() if receive new packets. The handler_running is a flag to check btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer() is exit.",
      "parentUuid": "bff58888_fa9e27cd",
      "revId": "dc221eacadea29481ac7fb8425f85be11077f89e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02b22a34_d7409e0e",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_sink.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 559,
      "author": {
        "id": 1994610
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T11:58:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer` can exit in 4 ways: The 3 `return`s, plus the break statement in the `while` loop.\n\nThe previous code had `timer_running \u003d 0` on all 4 paths.\n\n`btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer` has locked `g_mutex` from the beginning. So `btif_decode_alarm_cb` cannot get past `LockGuard lock(g_mutex);` while `btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer` is running.\n\nSo `btif_decode_alarm_cb` cannot run `if (timer_running \u003d\u003d 1)` while `btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer`\n\nSo I think my simplified code is equivalent to yours.\n\n-----\n\nIn 3 out of the 4 returns, rx_audio_queue will be empty (1st: already empty, 3rd: queue is flushed, 4th: breaks on NULL (empty)).\n\n------\n\nWhy do we need `timer_running` or `handler_running` at all?\n\nThis prevents more than one call to `btif_a2dp_sink_avk_handle_timer` from being queued at one time. This means that we can\u0027t temporarily prevent other tasks from running on the `worker_thread`.",
      "parentUuid": "f03422d1_0f82adba",
      "revId": "dc221eacadea29481ac7fb8425f85be11077f89e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "155c92f9_55c5b5c7",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_sink.cc",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1994610
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T13:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\n  LockGuard lock(g_mutex);\n  /* Allow this function to be queued when we exit this lock */\n  timer_running \u003d 0;\n\n  BT_HDR* p_msg;\n  if (fixed_queue_is_empty(btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_audio_queue)) {\n    APPL_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: empty queue\", __func__);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  /* Don\u0027t do anything in case of focus not granted */\n  if (btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_focus_state \u003d\u003d BTIF_A2DP_SINK_FOCUS_NOT_GRANTED) {\n    APPL_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: skipping frames since focus is not present\",\n                     __func__);\n    return;\n  }\n  /* Play only in BTIF_A2DP_SINK_FOCUS_GRANTED case */\n  if (btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_flush) {\n    fixed_queue_flush(btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_audio_queue, osi_free);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  APPL_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: process frames begin\", __func__);\n  while (true) {\n    p_msg \u003d (BT_HDR*)fixed_queue_try_dequeue(btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_audio_queue);\n    if (p_msg \u003d\u003d NULL) {\n      break;\n    }\n    APPL_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: number of packets in queue %zu\", __func__,\n                     fixed_queue_length(btif_a2dp_sink_cb.rx_audio_queue));\n\n    /* Queue packet has less frames */\n    btif_a2dp_sink_handle_inc_media(p_msg);\n    osi_free(p_msg);\n  }\n  APPL_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: process frames end\", __func__);\n}\n```",
